1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:07,500
GST InvoiceNow 2026: Your Paper Invoice Archive. A guide for Singapore finance and compliance teams

2
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:13,183
InvoiceNow only governs invoices issued after a business goes live on it.

3
00:00:13,183 --> 00:00:20,560
Invoices, purchase orders and delivery orders from before that date still fall under IRAS and ACRA retention rules.

4
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:25,500
Adopting InvoiceNow does not erase the duty to keep your paper invoice trail.

5
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:31,805
From: 1 April 2026. Who is in scope: New voluntary GST registrants. From: 1 April 2028.

6
00:00:31,805 --> 00:00:39,183
Who is in scope: Newly compulsory registrants; existing registrants up to S$200,000 taxable supplies. From: 1 April 2029.

7
00:00:39,183 --> 00:00:48,024
Who is in scope: Taxable supplies up to S$1 million. From: 1 April 2030. Who is in scope: Taxable supplies up to S$4 million. From: 1 April 2031.

8
00:00:48,024 --> 00:00:51,500
Who is in scope: All remaining GST-registered businesses.

9
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:57,914
IRAS: keep business and accounting records, including invoices, for at least 5 years.

10
00:00:57,914 --> 00:01:08,169
ACRA: keep accounting records and supporting documents for at least 5 years from the relevant financial year. Many businesses use 7 years as a compliance buffer.

11
00:01:08,169 --> 00:01:12,500
The PDPA also limits how long personal data in invoices may be kept.

12
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:21,589
High-resolution scanning with OCR indexing by invoice number, vendor and financial year. Retention metadata tied to the right statutory clock.

13
00:01:21,589 --> 00:01:26,487
Retrieve any historical invoice quickly for an IRAS audit, ACRA inspection or dispute.

14
00:01:26,487 --> 00:01:31,500
For the most sensitive records, an archival microfilm layer adds an air-gapped backstop.

15
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:42,725
1. Audit the backlog: by financial year; flag records near the end of retention. 2. Scan and index first: the years still within an active retention period. 3.

16
00:01:42,725 --> 00:01:52,500
Apply retention metadata: so records can be disposed of when the window closes. 4. Consider microfilm: for permanent records of the most sensitive kind.

17
00:01:53,500 --> 00:02:03,814
Do I still need paper invoices after InvoiceNow? Yes, for invoices issued before your go-live date, for the full retention period. Can old invoices be digitised? Yes.

18
00:02:03,814 --> 00:02:10,462
Scans must stay legible and retrievable on request. Does Micrographics Data set up InvoiceNow software? No.

19
00:02:10,462 --> 00:02:14,500
We solve the paper backlog: scanning, OCR indexing and archiving.

